  "scope": "One disposable kind v0.32.0 cluster using its bundled kindnet and Kubernetes v1.36.1; four case-owned namespaces for training, inference, pipeline, and notebook, each with one non-root BusyBox client and one fixed-marker HTTP responder. The case verifies all 12 directed cross-class IPv4 TCP/8080 paths before policy, then applies namespace-wide default-deny ingress and egress plus explicit selector-based ingress and egress rules. Four cross-class directions are allowed (training<->pipeline, pipeline->inference, notebook->training); the remaining eight are denied. One same-class path per namespace is also permitted. No Services, DNS, external targets, IPv6, other protocols, system namespaces, hostNetwork/node paths, production CNI, or cluster-wide policies are evaluated. A failed negative probe is attributed only to the controlled policy scenario after baseline reachability, healthy case-owned endpoints, and repeated timeout outcomes; the Kubernetes API does not identify a specific policy drop.",
